.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-pages-pull - Download a page's custom HTML


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad pages pull  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Download the custom HTML a storefront page currently serves into a local file, so pull → edit → push is a real round trip: what you pull is exactly what was pushed.

.PP
Only pages that already have custom HTML can be pulled. For a rich-text page, or a profile without published custom HTML, use \fBgumroad pages scaffold\fR instead — it generates starter HTML from the page's current render.

.PP
Edit the file, check the result with \fBgumroad pages preview <file>\fR, then publish it with \fBgumroad pages push <slug> <file>\fR\&.

.PP
Use the slug "profile" to pull your profile landing page's published custom HTML.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	Overwrite the output file if it already exists

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for pull

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	Write the HTML to this path (- for stdout; defaults to \&.html)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad pages pull about
  gumroad pages pull about -o custom.html
  gumroad pages pull about -o -
  gumroad pages pull profile
  gumroad pages pull about --json --jq '.page.title'
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-pages(1)\fP
